1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
Speaker 1: Donald Trump wants to end birthright citizenship.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,160
Speaker 1: Left-wing media and Democrats are fighting it tooth and nail

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:09,160
Speaker 1: because illegals, indeed criminals, are their mother's milk.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,760
Speaker 1: Among Donald Trump's first avalanche of executive orders

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:15,000
Speaker 1: was one ending birthright citizenship,

6
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:18,340
Speaker 1: the policy where almost anybody born on U.S. soil

7
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:20,320
Speaker 1: automatically gets citizenship.

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,320
Speaker 1: The practice itself comes from a misreading of the 14th Amendment,

9
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:27,040
Speaker 1: which granted citizenship to freed slaves,

10
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,220
Speaker 1: specifically to, quote,

11
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,900
Speaker 1: all persons born in the United States

12
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,920
Speaker 1: and subject to the jurisdiction thereof.

13
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,860
Speaker 1: The key phrase here is subject to the jurisdiction.

14
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:39,980
Speaker 1: That's long been understood to exclude diplomats,

15
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,400
Speaker 1: so birth alone is not enough,

16
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:45,140
Speaker 1: but jurisdiction is actually a whole lot more limiting.

17
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,900
Speaker 1: Historian Tom Wood cites the authors of the 14th Amendment,

18
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:49,820
Speaker 1: who said, quote,

19
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,420
Speaker 1: this will not, of course, include persons born in the United States

20
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,560
Speaker 1: who are foreigners or aliens,

21
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:57,680
Speaker 1: because it only applies to people, quote,

22
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:01,080
Speaker 1: not owing allegiance to any foreign sovereignty.

23
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:05,200
Speaker 1: In other words, if you have citizenship of another country, say Mexico,

24
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:09,420
Speaker 1: you are not under the jurisdiction, according to the 14th.

25
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:09,900
Speaker 1: Why?

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,680
Speaker 1: Because the point of the 14th was to give citizenship to former slaves

27
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,780
Speaker 1: who held no other citizenship.

28
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:19,460
Speaker 1: Now, notably, for 50 years after the 14th,

29
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:21,980
Speaker 1: Indians were not given birthright citizenship,

30
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:25,600
Speaker 1: specifically because they were citizens of another nation,

31
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:27,360
Speaker 1: the Navajo, Comanche, Seminole.

32
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,740
Speaker 1: And when they were given birthright citizenship,

33
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:33,580
Speaker 1: it was by act of Congress, not the 14th.

34
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:37,140
Speaker 1: Of course, not only are legal subject to the jurisdiction of another country,

35
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:38,940
Speaker 1: they are in this country illegally.

36
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:41,940
Speaker 1: They are literally fugitives from the law,

37
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:44,880
Speaker 1: the very definition of not under the jurisdiction.

38
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,640
Speaker 1: Now, this all matters because so-called birthright citizenship

39
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:51,620
Speaker 1: is one of the most abused parts of our immigration system.

40
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:57,860
Speaker 1: Every year, roughly 622,000 people are born to non-citizen parents,

41
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,080
Speaker 1: of which 400,000 to illegals.

42
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,660
Speaker 1: That comes to one in six births in the country.

43
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:06,660
Speaker 1: In the case of illegals, anchor babies become a jackpot.

44
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:13,000
Speaker 1: One study found 75% of migrants from Guatemala and Mexico with children

45
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Speaker 1: are on federal welfare programs,

46
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:17,740
Speaker 1: adding up to hundreds of billions in costs.

47
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:20,360
Speaker 1: Indeed, we've heard stories from Biden's illegals

48
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:23,080
Speaker 1: where young women in shelters try to get knocked up

49
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:26,600
Speaker 1: by pretty much anybody to get that precious anchor baby,

50
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,360
Speaker 1: your tax dollars at work.

51
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:33,380
Speaker 1: The abuse extends to an estimated 40,000 so-called birth tourists

52
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:35,820
Speaker 1: who literally fly to America on vacation,

53
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,900
Speaker 1: give birth, and go home with the status of parents of an American citizen

54
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,900
Speaker 1: despite having spent mere days in the country.

55
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,780
Speaker 1: This is a full-on industry in China and Taiwan

56
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,660
Speaker 1: where pre-birthing centers are common,

57
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,700
Speaker 1: kind of an assisted care for pregnant women.

58
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:51,320
Speaker 1: But instead of doing it in China,

59
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,060
Speaker 1: they fly to a center in LA,

60
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,040
Speaker 1: fully staffed by Chinese,

61
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:57,780
Speaker 1: and presto, they get all the benefits of citizenship.

62
00:02:57,940 --> 00:03:01,820
Speaker 1: All in between the illegals, temporary visas like H-1Bs or students

63
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,840
Speaker 1: and birth tourists,

64
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:06,400
Speaker 1: one in six new Americans either should not be here

65
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:08,940
Speaker 1: or have almost no connection to the country.

66
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,300
Speaker 1: So it's next, brought to you by Unchain.com.

67
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:14,060
Speaker 1: The left will go to war on this because they know

68
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,940
Speaker 1: the vast majority of beneficiaries will vote left.

69
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:20,940
Speaker 1: The case they'll keep citing is Wong Kim Ark from 1873,

70
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:24,840
Speaker 1: which grants citizenship to the child of permanent residence,

71
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:27,480
Speaker 1: something most Americans are probably fine with

72
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,680
Speaker 1: and something that has nothing to do

73
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:34,400
Speaker 1: with these 622,000 illegals and tourists abusing the system.

74
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,260
Speaker 1: Okay, we'll be watching.

75
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:37,320
Speaker 1: See you next time.
